 "text": "Song stuck in your head? Grab a piece of gum. In 2015, psychologists at the University of Reading played people catchy pop songs. Then they asked them not to think about them. People chewing gum heard the song in their heads less often. Here's the trick. Replaying a song uses your inner voice, like silently singing. Chewing jams that system. Less room for the chorus. So, next time it's on repeat. Chew. Follow for more mind tricks.",
